factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The reel_script says the Chennai–Kollam train runs 'via Podanur' in its opening line and the headline frames all trains as via Podanur, but the article only says Podanur is one stop of the Chennai–Kollam train and makes the Darbhanga train's destination Podanur; the reel_script's claim that the Chennai–Kollam trains are 'Podanur vazhiyaaga' is a framing not directly stated, though Podanur is listed as a stop.
  The reel_script states the Kollam-to-Chennai train stops at Podanur, Tiruppur, Salem, Palakkad and Katpadi, but omits Erode, Arakkonam, Tiruvallur and Perambur listed in the article.
  The reel_script's Darbhanga sentence says the train 'இயக்கப்படுகிறது' from Darbhanga to Podanur and then attributes the arrival time to Southern Railway; the article attributes the whole train announcement to Southern Railway, which is consistent, but the reel_script's Darbhanga train is said to arrive at Podanur without mentioning its stops (Parbhani, Dhanbad, Ranchi, Vijayawada, Katpadi, Salem, Erode, Tiruppur), an important omission of route information present in the article.
  The reel_script states the Chennai-Kollam train runs 'சென்னை எழும்பூர் மற்றும் கொல்லம் இடையே' which is accurate, but the caption/slides say 'Nov 19' and 'Nov 20', 'Nov 18' dates; the article gives only the day numbers (19, 20, 18) without naming the month, so the month 'நவம்பர்' is an invented detail not in the article.
